The '''2023–24 season''' was the 116th season in the existence of [[Inter Milan]], which have all been played in the top division of [[Football in Italy|Italian football]]. In addition to the [[2023–24 Serie A|domestic league]], Inter participated in this season's editions of the [[2023–24 Coppa Italia|Coppa Italia]], the [[2023 Supercoppa Italiana|Supercoppa Italiana]] and the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].

This season was the first since [[2011–12 Inter Milan season|2011–12]] without Slovenian goalkeeper [[Samir Handanović]], who announced his departure following the end of his contract, the first since [[2013–14 Inter Milan season|2013–14]] without centre-back [[Danilo D'Ambrosio]] who departed the ''Nerazzurri'' club to join [[AC Monza|Monza]], and the first since [[2014–15 Inter Milan season|2014–15]] without Croatian midfielder [[Marcelo Brozović]], who also left after being transferred to Saudi Arabian club [[Al Nassr FC|Al Nassr]].

On 20 December, Coppa Italia defending champions suffered a 1–2 loss after extra time against [[Bologna FC 1909|Bologna]] in the round of 16, getting knocked out of the competition. On 22 January, the ''Nerazzurri'' clinched their third consecutive Supercoppa Italiana by defeating [[SS Lazio|Lazio]] 3–0 in the semi-finals and [[SSC Napoli|Napoli]] 1–0 in the final. After reaching the [[2023 UEFA Champions League final|final]] in the [[2022–23 UEFA Champions League|2022–23 edition]], Inter's Champions League campaign was cut short on 13 March by getting knocked out at the round of 16 stage by [[Atlético Madrid]]. After drawing on aggregate 2–2, the ''Colchoneros'' went on to win the deciding penalty shoot-out 3–2. On 22 April, with five games to spare, Inter were mathematically confirmed as Serie A champions for the twentieth time in their history after defeating second-placed and city rivals [[AC Milan]] in the [[Derby della Madonnina]], earning the second [[Star (sport badge)|star]] above their badge.

